eine-dependent life isn''t easy."}, {"name": "~는 것 같다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Conjecture/appearance marker. ~는 것 nominalizes; 같다 adds epistemic hedge ''seems/appears to.''", "ex_ko": "카페인에 의존하는 생활에서 벗어나는 것이 쉽지 않다는 점에서 많은 사람들이 공감하는 것 같습니다.", "ex_en": "Many people seem to relate, since breaking away from a caffeine-dependent life isn''t easy."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''Can; may'': 방해하다 → 방해할 수 있다 ''can disturb''.", "ex_ko": "특히 피로를 커피로 해결하는 습관이 오히려 수면을 방해할 수 있다는 점은 눈여겨볼 만합니다.", "ex_en": "In particular, it''s worth noting that the habit of fighting fatigue with coffee can actually disturb sleep."}, {"name": "~다는 점", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Nominalizes proposition to treat it as ''the point/fact that.'' Shifts emphasis to content itself.", "ex_ko": "특히 피로를 커피로 해결하는 습관이 오히려 수면을 방해할 수 있다는 점은 눈여겨볼 만합니다.", "ex_en": "In particular, it''s worth noting that the habit of fighting fatigue with coffee can actually disturb sleep."}, {"name": "~(으)면서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''As / along with'': 개선되다 → 개선되면서 ''as (sleep) improves, (your condition) also…''.", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 카페인 섭취를 줄이면 수면의 질이 개선되면서 전반적인 컨디션이 좋아질 수 있다고 말합니다.", "ex_en": "Experts say that cutting down on caffeine can improve sleep quality and, with it, your overall condition."}, {"name": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Possibility marker. 좋아지다 + ㄹ 수 있다 signals potential or capacity.", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 카페인 섭취를 줄이면 수면의 질이 개선되면서 전반적인 컨디션이 좋아질 수 있다고 말합니다.", "ex_en": "Experts say that cutting down on caffeine can improve sleep quality and, with it, your overall condition."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mvr7fl3vun8f' and md5(translation) = '6ada8d81749f1915f334f194db92dfdc';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Solar power generation is establishing itself as a key driver of global energy transition. Solar has now overtaken nuclear power generation and become the fastest-growing energy source.", "As the amount of electricity produced by solar panels increases significantly, existing energy sources are falling behind in the competition. Even nuclear power plants appear unable to keep pace with solar''s rapid growth rate.", "Experts emphasize that \"solar power is now the engine of energy transition.\" Solar has gained this level of influence because production costs have steadily decreased along with technological advances.", "If solar power generation expands further, major changes are expected across the entire power system. Countries are actively moving forward with expanding renewable energy, including solar, to reduce carbon emissions."], "sentences": [{"text": "태양광 발전이 전 세계 전력 전환의 핵심 동력으로 자리잡고 있습니다.", "translation": "Solar power generation is establishing itself as a key driver of global energy transition.", "vocab": [{"ko": "태양광", "en": "solar power", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발전", "en": "generation; development", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전환", "en": "transition; shift", "note": ""}, {"ko": "핵심", "en": "core; key", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "progressive aspect. Indicates ongoing action or state. 자리잡다 → 자리잡고 있다 (is establishing itself).", "example_in_sentence": "자리잡고 있습니다"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)로 자리잡다", "exp": "''To become established as N'': 핵심 동력으로 자리잡다 ''establish itself as a key driver''.", "example_in_sentence": "동력으로 자리잡고"}]}, {"text": "태양광은 이제 원자력 발전을 제치고 가장 빠르게 성장하는 에너지원이 되었다고 합니다.", "translation": "Solar has now reportedly overtaken nuclear power to become the fastest-growing energy source.", "vocab": [{"ko": "원자력", "en": "nuclear power", "note": ""}, {"ko": "제치다", "en": "to overtake; to surpass", "note": ""}, {"ko": "성장", "en": "growth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "에너지원", "en": "energy source", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게", "exp": "adverbializer suffix. Forms adverbs from adjectives. 빠르다 → 빠르게 (quickly).", "example_in_sentence": "빠르게"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~을/를 제치고", "exp": "overtake; surpass; outpace. Indicates surpassing or going beyond something/someone.", "example_in_sentence": "원자력 발전을 제치고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 하다", "exp": "Reports information: 되다 → 되었다고 합니다 ''(it) is said to have become''.", "example_in_sentence": "에너지원이 되었다고 합니다"}]}, {"text": "태양광 패널이 생산하는 전력량이 크게 늘어나면서 기존 에너지원들이 경쟁에서 뒤처지게 되었습니다.", "translation": "As the amount of electricity produced by solar panels increases significantly, existing energy sources are falling behind in the competition.", "vocab": [{"ko": "패널", "en": "panel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생산하다", "en": "to produce", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전력량", "en": "amount of electricity", "note": ""}, {"ko": "늘어나다", "en": "to increase", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면서", "exp": "simultaneous action. Two events occur at the same time. 늘어나면서 (while increasing / as it increases).", "example_in_sentence": "늘어나면서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다", "exp": "''End up / come to'': 뒤처지다 → 뒤처지게 되었습니다 ''ended up falling behind''.", "example_in_sentence": "뒤처지게 되었습니다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게", "exp": "adverbializer suffix. Forms adverbs from adjectives. 크다 → 크게 (greatly; significantly).", "example_in_sentence": "크게"}]}, {"text": "원자력 발전소조차 태양광의 급격한 성장 속도를 따라가지 못하고 있는 것 같습니다.", "translation": "Even nuclear power plants appear unable to keep pace with solar''s rapid growth rate.", "vocab": [{"ko": "발전소", "en": "power plant", "note": ""}, {"ko": "급격하다", "en": "to be rapid; to be sudden", "note": ""}, {"ko": "속도", "en": "speed; rate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "따라가다", "en": "to keep up with; to follow", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~조차", "exp": "emphatic particle. Emphasizes inclusion, often with negation or surprise. 원자력 발전소조차 (even nuclear power plants).", "example_in_sentence": "발전소조차"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 못하다", "exp": "Negative ''cannot'': 따라가다 → 따라가지 못하다 ''cannot keep up''.", "example_in_sentence": "따라가지 못하고"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~는 것 같다", "exp": "''Seems (to be)'': 못하고 있다 → 못하고 있는 것 같습니다 ''seem to be unable''.", "example_in_sentence": "있는 것 같습니다"}]}, {"text": "전문가들은 \"태양광은 이제 전력 전환의 엔진\"이라고 강조합니다.", "translation": "Experts emphasize that \"solar power is now the engine of energy transition.\"", "vocab": [{"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "엔진", "en": "engine", "note": ""}, {"ko": "강조하다", "en": "to emphasize; to stress", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라고 강조하다", "exp": "Reports a quoted statement after a noun: \"…엔진\"이라고 강조합니다 ''emphasize that (it) is \"the engine…\"''.", "example_in_sentence": "엔진\"이라고 강조합니다"}]}, {"text": "태양광이 이 정도의 영향력을 갖게 된 것은 기술 발전과 함께 생산 비용이 꾸준히 낮아졌기 때문입니다.", "translation": "Solar has gained this level of influence because production costs have steadily decreased along with technological advances.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정도", "en": "degree; extent; level", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영향력", "en": "influence; impact", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기술", "en": "technology; technique", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비용", "en": "cost; expense", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다", "exp": "''Come to'': 가지다 → 갖게 되다 ''come to have'' → 갖게 된 것은 ''the fact that (solar) came to have''.", "example_in_sentence": "갖게 된"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와", "exp": "with; accompaniment. Marks cooperation or joint action. 기술 발전과 함께 (together with technological advances).", "example_in_sentence": "발전과"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~히", "exp": "Makes an adverb from many 하다 adjectives: 꾸준하다 ''to be steady'' → 꾸준히 ''steadily''.", "example_in_sentence": "꾸준히"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~기 때문이다", "exp": "''It''s because…'': 낮아지다 → 낮아졌기 때문입니다 ''because (costs) have fallen''.", "example_in_sentence": "낮아졌기 때문입니다"}]}, {"text": "태양광 발전이 더욱 확대되면 전력 시스템 전체에 큰 변화가 생길 전망입니다.", "translation": "If solar power generation expands further, major changes are expected across the entire power system.", "vocab": [{"ko": "확대하다", "en": "to expand; to enlarge", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시스템", "en": "system", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전체", "en": "whole; entire", "note": ""}, {"ko": "변화", "en": "change; transformation", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "conditional. If/when something happens. 확대되면 (if it expands).", "example_in_sentence": "확대되면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 전망이다", "exp": "''Is expected to'': 생기다 → 생길 전망입니다 ''(big changes) are expected to come''.", "example_in_sentence": "생길 전망입니다"}]}, {"text": "각국은 탄소 배출을 줄이기 위해 태양광을 비롯한 재생에너지 확대에 적극 나서고 있습니다.", "translation": "Countries are actively moving forward with expanding renewable energy, including solar, to reduce carbon emissions.", "vocab": [{"ko": "각국", "en": "each country; various countries", "note": ""}, {"ko": "탄소", "en": "carbon", "note": ""}, {"ko": "배출", "en": "emission", "note": ""}, {"ko": "줄이다", "en": "to reduce; to cut down", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해(서)", "exp": "in order to / for the purpose of. Expresses purpose or intention. 줄이기 위해 (in order to reduce).", "example_in_sentence": "줄이기 위해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 비롯한", "exp": "including / starting with. Introduces a leading example in a list. 태양광을 비롯한 (including solar).", "example_in_sentence": "태양광을 비롯한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "progressive aspect. Ongoing action or state. 나서고 있다 (are actively taking action).", "example_in_sentence": "나서고 있습니다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "태양광", "en": "solar power", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발전", "en": "generation; development", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전환", "en": "transition; shift", "note": ""}, {"ko": "핵심", "en": "core; key", "note": ""}, {"ko": "원자력", "en": "nuclear power", "note": ""}, {"ko": "제치다", "en": "to overtake; to surpass", "note": ""}, {"ko": "성장", "en": "growth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "에너지원", "en": "energy source", "note": ""}, {"ko": "패널", "en": "panel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생산하다", "en": "to produce", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전력량", "en": "amount of electricity", "note": ""}, {"ko": "늘어나다", "en": "to increase", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발전소", "en": "power plant", "note": ""}, {"ko": "급격하다", "en": "to be rapid; to be sudden", "note": ""}, {"ko": "속도", "en": "speed; rate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "따라가다", "en": "to keep up with; to follow", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "엔진", "en": "engine", "note": ""}, {"ko": "강조하다", "en": "to emphasize; to stress", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정도", "en": "degree; extent; level", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영향력", "en": "influence; impact", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기술", "en": "technology; technique", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비용", "en": "cost; expense", "note": ""}, {"ko": "확대하다", "en": "to expand; to enlarge", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시스템", "en": "system", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전체", "en": "whole; entire", "note": ""}, {"ko": "변화", "en": "change; transformation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "각국", "en": "each country; various countries", "note": ""}, {"ko": "탄소", "en": "carbon", "note": ""}, {"ko": "배출", "en": "emission", "note": ""}, {"ko": "줄이다", "en": "to reduce; to cut down", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~고 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "progressive aspect. Indicates ongoing action or state. 자리잡다 → 자리잡고 있다 (is establishing itself).", "ex_ko": "태양광 발전이 전 세계 전력 전환의 핵심 동력으로 자리잡고 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Solar power generation is establishing itself as a key driver of global energy transition."}, {"name": "~게", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "adverbializer suffix. Forms adverbs from adjectives. 크다 → 크게 (greatly; significantly).", "ex_ko": "태양광은 이제 원자력 발전을 제치고 가장 빠르게 성장하는 에너지원이 되었다고 합니다.", "ex_en": "Solar has now reportedly overtaken nuclear power to become the fastest-growing energy source."}, {"name": "~다고 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reports information: 되다 → 되었다고 합니다 ''(it) is said to have become''.", "ex_ko": "태양광은 이제 원자력 발전을 제치고 가장 빠르게 성장하는 에너지원이 되었다고 합니다.", "ex_en": "Solar has now reportedly overtaken nuclear power to become the fastest-growing energy source."}, {"name": "~(으)면서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "simultaneous action. Two events occur at the same time. 늘어나면서 (while increasing / as it increases).", "ex_ko": "태양광 패널이 생산하는 전력량이 크게 늘어나면서 기존 에너지원들이 경쟁에서 뒤처지게 되었습니다.", "ex_en": "As the amount of electricity produced by solar panels increases significantly, existing energy sources are falling behind in the competition."}, {"name": "~게 되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''Come to'': 가지다 → 갖게 되다 ''come to have'' → 갖게 된 것은 ''the fact that (solar) came to have''.", "ex_ko": "태양광 패널이 생산하는 전력량이 크게 늘어나면서 기존 에너지원들이 경쟁에서 뒤처지게 되었습니다.", "ex_en": "As the amount of electricity produced by solar panels increases significantly, existing energy sources are falling behind in the competition."}, {"name": "~조차", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "emphatic particle. Emphasizes inclusion, often with negation or surprise. 원자력 발전소조차 (even nuclear power plants).", "ex_ko": "원자력 발전소조차 태양광의 급격한 성장 속도를 따라가지 못하고 있는 것 같습니다.", "ex_en": "Even nuclear power plants appear unable to keep pace with solar''s rapid growth rate."}, {"name": "~지 못하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Negative ''cannot'': 따라가다 → 따라가지 못하다 ''cannot keep up''.", "ex_ko": "원자력 발전소조차 태양광의 급격한 성장 속도를 따라가지 못하고 있는 것 같습니다.", "ex_en": "Even nuclear power plants appear unable to keep pace with solar''s rapid growth rate."}, {"name": "~(이)라고 강조하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reports a quoted statement after a noun: \"…엔진\"이라고 강조합니다 ''emphasize that (it) is \"the engine…\"''.", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 \"태양광은 이제 전력 전환의 엔진\"이라고 강조합니다.", "ex_en": "Experts emphasize that \"solar power is now the engine of energy transition.\""}, {"name": "~과/와", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "with; accompaniment. Marks cooperation or joint action. 기술 발전과 함께 (together with technological advances).", "ex_ko": "태양광이 이 정도의 영향력을 갖게 된 것은 기술 발전과 함께 생산 비용이 꾸준히 낮아졌기 때문입니다.", "ex_en": "Solar has gained this level of influence because production costs have steadily decreased along with technological advances."}, {"name": "~히", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Makes an adverb from many 하다 adjectives: 꾸준하다 ''to be steady'' → 꾸준히 ''steadily''.", "ex_ko": "태양광이 이 정도의 영향력을 갖게 된 것은 기술 발전과 함께 생산 비용이 꾸준히 낮아졌기 때문입니다.", "ex_en": "Solar has gained this level of influence because production costs have steadily decreased along with technological advances."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 전망이다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''Is expected to'': 생기다 → 생길 전망입니다 ''(big changes) are expected to come''.", "ex_ko": "태양광 발전이 더욱 확대되면 전력 시스템 전체에 큰 변화가 생길 전망입니다.", "ex_en": "If solar power generation expands further, major changes are expected across the entire power system."}, {"name": "~기 위해(서)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "in order to / for the purpose of. Expresses purpose or intention. 줄이기 위해 (in order to reduce).", "ex_ko": "각국은 탄소 배출을 줄이기 위해 태양광을 비롯한 재생에너지 확대에 적극 나서고 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Countries are actively moving forward with expanding renewable energy, including solar, to reduce carbon emissions."}, {"name": "~을/를 비롯한", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "including / starting with. Introduces a leading example in a list. 태양광을 비롯한 (including solar).", "ex_ko": "각국은 탄소 배출을 줄이기 위해 태양광을 비롯한 재생에너지 확대에 적극 나서고 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Countries are actively moving forward with expanding renewable energy, including solar, to reduce carbon emissions."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mvro6davzi74' and md5(translation) = 'ec97a4f73353d28bd572367593f055fe';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Former BIGBANG member Seungri spoke directly about his wife and child. Seungri, who typically doesn''t talk much about his family, opened up this time.", "Seungri publicly shared stories about his wife and child. People showed a lot of interest in this news.", "It is known that this is the first time Seungri has directly spoken about his family. His remarks drew attention from people who had been curious about Seungri''s family news up until now."], "sentences": [{"text": "빅뱅의 전 멤버 승리가 아내와 아이에 대해 직접 이야기했어요.", "translation": "Former BIGBANG member Seungri spoke directly about his wife and child.", "vocab": [{"ko": "멤버", "en": "member", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아내", "en": "wife", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아이", "en": "child", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이야기하다", "en": "to talk, to speak", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive / relational)", "exp": "genitive marker. Possession use: 빅뱅 (BIGBANG) → 빅뱅의 전 멤버 (BIGBANG''s former member).", "example_in_sentence": "빅뱅의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "subject particle marking the agent. 승리 (Seungri) + 가 = the subject of the action.", "example_in_sentence": "승리가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와 (with — comitative / and — listing)", "exp": "listing use; connects nouns in a coordinate phrase. 아내 (wife) + 와 + 아이 (child) = wife and child.", "example_in_sentence": "아내와 아이에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 대해(서)/대한 (about)", "exp": "topical particle. About/regarding. 아내와 아이 (wife and child) + 에 대해 (about) = about his wife and child.", "example_in_sentence": "아내와 아이에 대해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 하다 verbs become 했어요: 이야기하다 → 이야기했어요 ''talked''.", "example_in_sentence": "이야기했어요"}]}, {"text": "평소에 가족 이야기를 잘 하지 않던 승리였지만, 이번에는 직접 입을 열었어요.", "translation": "Seungri, who usually didn''t talk about his family, spoke up himself this time.", "vocab": [{"ko": "평소", "en": "usually, typically, normally", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가족", "en": "family", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이야기", "en": "story, talk, conversation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하다", "en": "to do", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (location / time / direction / target)", "exp": "time point marker. When/during. 평소 (usual time) + 에 = during usual times, normally.", "example_in_sentence": "평소에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "direct object particle. 이야기 (story/talk) + 를 = direct object of the verb 하다 (do/talk).", "example_in_sentence": "이야기를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~던 (retrospective modifier)", "exp": "past habitual/unfinished action modifying a noun. 하지 않다 (not do) + 던 (used to/was being) → 하지 않던 승리 (Seungri, who was not talking).", "example_in_sentence": "하지 않던"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지만 (but)", "exp": "contrast conjunction. Despite (characteristic); but/however. 승리였지만 (Seungri was [that way], but...) signals contrast with the second clause.", "example_in_sentence": "승리였지만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에는 (contrast)", "exp": "에 + 는 adds contrast: 이번에는 ''this time (unlike before)''.", "example_in_sentence": "이번에는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 열다 → 열었어요 ''opened''.", "example_in_sentence": "열었어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "입을 열다", "exp": "to open one''s mouth; idiom meaning to speak up, to break silence.", "example_in_sentence": "입을 열었어요"}]}, {"text": "승리는 자신의 아내와 아이에 대한 이야기를 공개적으로 했어요.", "translation": "Seungri publicly shared stories about his wife and child.", "vocab": [{"ko": "자신", "en": "oneself, himself, herself", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아내", "en": "wife", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아이", "en": "child", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이야기", "en": "story, talk", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "topic particle. 승리 (Seungri) + 는 = as for Seungri (establishing topic).", "example_in_sentence": "승리는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive / relational)", "exp": "genitive marker, possession use. 자신 (oneself) + 의 = his own.", "example_in_sentence": "자신의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와 (with — comitative / and — listing)", "exp": "listing use; connects nouns. 아내 (wife) + 와 + 아이 (child) = wife and child.", "example_in_sentence": "아내와 아이에"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~에 대한 N", "exp": "''About N'' before a noun: 아내와 아이에 대한 이야기 ''a story about his wife and child''.", "example_in_sentence": "아내와 아이에 대한 이야기"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "direct object particle. 이야기 (story) + 를 = direct object of 하다 (do/share).", "example_in_sentence": "이야기를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~적으로", "exp": "~적 ''-ic / -al'' + (으)로 makes an adverb: 공개적 ''public'' → 공개적으로 ''publicly''.", "example_in_sentence": "공개적으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 하다 → 했어요 ''did (talk)''.", "example_in_sentence": "했어요"}]}, {"text": "사람들은 이 소식에 많은 관심을 보였어요.", "translation": "People showed a lot of interest in this news.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사람", "en": "person, people", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소식", "en": "news, information, word", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many, to be much", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관심", "en": "interest, attention, concern", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "topic particle. 사람들 (people) + 은 = as for people (establishing topic).", "example_in_sentence": "사람들은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (location / time / direction / target)", "exp": "target-of-interest marker. 소식 (news) + 에 (toward/at) = focused on/toward the news.", "example_in_sentence": "소식에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은 (past verb / present adj modifier)", "exp": "present adjective modifying noun. 많다 (to be many) + ㄴ → 많은 (many). Modifies 관심 (interest).", "example_in_sentence": "많은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "direct object particle. 관심 (interest) + 을 = direct object of 보이다 (show).", "example_in_sentence": "관심을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 보이다 ''to show'' → 보였어요 (이 + 었 → 였) ''showed''.", "example_in_sentence": "보였어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "관심을 보이다", "exp": "to show interest; collocation expressing display of attention or concern.", "example_in_sentence": "관심을 보였어요"}]}, {"text": "승리가 가족에 대해 직접 말한 것은 이번이 처음으로 알려져 있어요.", "translation": "It is known that this is the first time Seungri has directly spoken about his family.", "vocab": [{"ko": "가족", "en": "family", "note": ""}, {"ko": "말하다", "en": "to speak, to say, to talk", "note": ""}, {"ko": "것", "en": "thing, fact, matter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "처음", "en": "first time, first, beginning", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "subject particle. 승리 (Seungri) + 가 = subject of the action of speaking.", "example_in_sentence": "승리가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 대해(서)/대한 (about)", "exp": "topical particle. 가족 (family) + 에 대해 (about/regarding) = about/concerning family.", "example_in_sentence": "가족에 대해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은 (past verb / present adj modifier)", "exp": "past verb modifier. 말하다 (to speak) + ㄴ → 말한 (spoke, having spoken). Modifies 것 (thing/fact).", "example_in_sentence": "말한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle: 말한 것은 ''the fact that (he) spoke…'' is the topic of the sentence.", "example_in_sentence": "것은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "subject particle. 이번 (this time) + 이 = this time is the subject of being first.", "example_in_sentence": "이번이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 알려져 있다", "exp": "''Is known as / to be'': 알다 → 알려지다 ''become known'' → 알려져 있다 ''is known''. 처음으로 알려져 있어요 ''is known to be the first time''.", "example_in_sentence": "처음으로 알려져 있어요"}]}, {"text": "그동안 승리의 가족 소식을 알고 싶어 하던 사람들에게 이번 발언은 주목을 받았어요.", "translation": "His remarks drew attention from people who had been curious about Seungri''s family news up until now.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그동안", "en": "up until now, meanwhile, all this time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소식", "en": "news, information, word", "note": ""}, {"ko": "알다", "en": "to know, to understand, to learn", "note": ""}, {"ko": "싶다", "en": "to want to, to wish", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive / relational)", "exp": "genitive marker, possession use. 승리 (Seungri) + 의 = Seungri''s.", "example_in_sentence": "승리의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "direct object particle. 소식 (news) + 을 = direct object of 알다 (know) and 싶다 (want).", "example_in_sentence": "소식을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~던 (retrospective modifier)", "exp": "past habitual/unfinished action modifying noun. 알고 싶어 하다 (want to know) + 던 (used to, was being) → 알고 싶어 하던 사람들 (people who had been wanting to know).", "example_in_sentence": "싶어 하던"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게/한테 (to person)", "exp": "indirect object marker for animate recipient. 사람들 (people) + 에게 = to the people.", "example_in_sentence": "사람들에게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "topic particle. 발언 (remark) + 은 = as for this remark (establishing topic).", "example_in_sentence": "발언은"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "주목을 받다", "exp": "''To draw attention'': 주목 ''attention'' + 을 받다 ''receive'' → 주목을 받았어요 ''drew attention''.", "example_in_sentence": "주목을 받았어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 받다 → 받았어요 ''received''.", "example_in_sentence": "받았어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "멤버", "en": "member", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아내", "en": "wife", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아이", "en": "child", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이야기하다", "en": "to talk, to speak", "note": ""}, {"ko": "평소", "en": "usually, typically, normally", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가족", "en": "family", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이야기", "en": "story, talk, conversat