polite ending. 하다 verbs become 했어요: 이야기하다 → 이야기했어요 ''talked''.", "ex_ko": "빅뱅의 전 멤버 승리가 아내와 아이에 대해 직접 이야기했어요.", "ex_en": "Former BIGBANG member Seungri spoke directly about his wife and child."}, {"name": "~에 (location / time / direction / target)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "time point marker. When/during. 평소 (usual time) + 에 = during usual times, normally.", "ex_ko": "평소에 가족 이야기를 잘 하지 않던 승리였지만, 이번에는 직접 입을 열었어요.", "ex_en": "Seungri, who usually didn''t talk about his family, spoke up himself this time."}, {"name": "~을/를 (object marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "direct object particle. 이야기 (story/talk) + 를 = direct object of the verb 하다 (do/talk).", "ex_ko": "평소에 가족 이야기를 잘 하지 않던 승리였지만, 이번에는 직접 입을 열었어요.", "ex_en": "Seungri, who usually didn''t talk about his family, spoke up himself this time."}, {"name": "~던 (retrospective modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "past habitual/unfinished action modifying noun. 알고 싶어 하다 (want to know) + 던 (used to, was being) → 알고 싶어 하던 사람들 (people who had been wanting to know).", "ex_ko": "평소에 가족 이야기를 잘 하지 않던 승리였지만, 이번에는 직접 입을 열었어요.", "ex_en": "Seungri, who usually didn''t talk about his family, spoke up himself this time."}, {"name": "~지만 (but)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "contrast conjunction. Despite (characteristic); but/however. 승리였지만 (Seungri was [that way], but...) signals contrast with the second clause.", "ex_ko": "평소에 가족 이야기를 잘 하지 않던 승리였지만, 이번에는 직접 입을 열었어요.", "ex_en": "Seungri, who usually didn''t talk about his family, spoke up himself this time."}, {"name": "~에는 (contrast)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "에 + 는 adds contrast: 이번에는 ''this time (unlike before)''.", "ex_ko": "평소에 가족 이야기를 잘 하지 않던 승리였지만, 이번에는 직접 입을 열었어요.", "ex_en": "Seungri, who usually didn''t talk about his family, spoke up himself this time."}, {"name": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Topic particle: 말한 것은 ''the fact that (he) spoke…'' is the topic of the sentence.", "ex_ko": "승리는 자신의 아내와 아이에 대한 이야기를 공개적으로 했어요.", "ex_en": "Seungri publicly shared stories about his wife and child."}, {"name": "~적으로", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "~적 ''-ic / -al'' + (으)로 makes an adverb: 공개적 ''public'' → 공개적으로 ''publicly''.", "ex_ko": "승리는 자신의 아내와 아이에 대한 이야기를 공개적으로 했어요.", "ex_en": "Seungri publicly shared stories about his wife and child."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/은 (past verb / present adj modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "past verb modifier. 말하다 (to speak) + ㄴ → 말한 (spoke, having spoken). Modifies 것 (thing/fact).", "ex_ko": "사람들은 이 소식에 많은 관심을 보였어요.", "ex_en": "People showed a lot of interest in this news."}, {"name": "~(으)로 알려져 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''Is known as / to be'': 알다 → 알려지다 ''become known'' → 알려져 있다 ''is known''. 처음으로 알려져 있어요 ''is known to be the first time''.", "ex_ko": "승리가 가족에 대해 직접 말한 것은 이번이 처음으로 알려져 있어요.", "ex_en": "It is known that this is the first time Seungri has directly spoken about his family."}, {"name": "~에게/한테 (to person)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "indirect object marker for animate recipient. 사람들 (people) + 에게 = to the people.", "ex_ko": "그동안 승리의 가족 소식을 알고 싶어 하던 사람들에게 이번 발언은 주목을 받았어요.", "ex_en": "His remarks drew attention from people who had been curious about Seungri''s family news up until now."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mvro9y6205aj' and md5(translation) = '520149c38973d81ef5a8453ff380d24c';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Dad Matt MacMillan collected his baby Ryan''s sounds, recording them for a full year.", "He used those sounds to recreate the rock song ''Thunderstruck'' by AC/DC.", "The baby''s sounds were not altered — the pitches were used exactly as recorded, and 83 clips were usable.", "The dad found the notes by plucking them out on a piano, then matched them to the baby''s sounds, which took a very long time.", "The video has been viewed over 11 million times and many people love it.", "This was not his first baby-sound music project — he previously made a song using baby Ella''s sounds as well."], "sentences": [{"text": "아빠 맷 맥밀런은 아기 라이언의 소리를 모았어요.", "translation": "Dad Matt McMillan collected baby Ryan''s sounds.", "vocab": [{"ko": "아빠", "en": "dad"}, {"ko": "소리", "en": "sound"}, {"ko": "모으다", "en": "to collect"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "1년 동안 아기 소리를 녹음했어요.", "translation": "He recorded the baby''s sounds for a year.", "vocab": [{"ko": "1년", "en": "one year"}, {"ko": "동안", "en": "during"}, {"ko": "녹음하다", "en": "to record"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "N 동안 (during)", "exp": "Time duration marker. Indicates the period or span in which action occurs.", "example_in_sentence": "1년 동안"}]}, {"text": "아빠는 그 소리로 록 음악을 만들었어요.", "translation": "Dad made rock music from those sounds.", "vocab": [{"ko": "소리", "en": "sound"}, {"ko": "록 음악", "en": "rock music"}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (material)", "exp": "Marks what something is made with: 그 소리로 음악을 만들다 ''make music with those sounds''.", "example_in_sentence": "소리로"}]}, {"text": "AC/DC의 ''썬더스트럭''이에요.", "translation": "It is AC/DC''s ''Thunderstruck''.", "vocab": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "아기 소리는 바꾸지 않았어요.", "translation": "The baby sounds were not changed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바꾸다", "en": "to change"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "Negative ''did not'': 바꾸다 → 바꾸지 않았어요 ''didn''t change''.", "example_in_sentence": "바꾸지 않았어요"}]}, {"text": "높낮이를 그대로 썼어요.", "translation": "He kept the pitch exactly as it was.", "vocab": [{"ko": "높낮이", "en": "pitch, tone"}, {"ko": "그대로", "en": "as is, unchanged"}, {"ko": "쓰다", "en": "to use, to write"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "쓸 수 있는 소리는 83개였어요.", "translation": "There were 83 sounds that could be used.", "vocab": [{"ko": "쓰다", "en": "to use"}, {"ko": "개", "en": "counter for objects"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "''Can'': 쓰다 → 쓸 수 있다; as a noun modifier: 쓸 수 있는 소리 ''sounds that could be used''.", "example_in_sentence": "쓸 수 있는"}]}, {"text": "아빠는 피아노로 음을 찾았어요.", "translation": "Dad found the notes using a piano.", "vocab": [{"ko": "피아노", "en": "piano"}, {"ko": "음", "en": "note, musical tone"}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to find"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (tool)", "exp": "Marks the tool used: 피아노로 ''with / on a piano''.", "example_in_sentence": "피아노로"}]}, {"text": "그리고 아기 소리와 맞췄어요.", "translation": "Then he matched them to the baby''s sounds.", "vocab": [{"ko": "맞추다", "en": "to match, to align"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~와/과 맞추다", "exp": "''Match (something) to N'': 아기 소리와 맞추다 ''match (the notes) to the baby''s sounds''.", "example_in_sentence": "소리와"}]}, {"text": "아주 오래 걸렸어요.", "translation": "It took a very long time.", "vocab": [{"ko": "아주", "en": "very, quite"}, {"ko": "오래", "en": "long time"}, {"ko": "걸리다", "en": "to take (time)"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "영상을 1,100만 명이 넘게 봤어요.", "translation": "More than 11 million people watched the video.", "vocab": [{"ko": "영상", "en": "video"}, {"ko": "명", "en": "counter for people"}, {"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed, to go over"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to watch, to see"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게", "exp": "Makes an adverb: 넘다 ''to exceed'' → 넘게 ''over / more than'': 1,100만 명이 넘게 ''more than 11 million people''.", "example_in_sentence": "넘게"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 좋아해요.", "translation": "Many people like it.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; to be a lot"}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person"}, {"ko": "좋아하다", "en": "to like"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 아기 소리 음악은 처음이 아니에요.", "translation": "This isn''t his first music made from baby sounds.", "vocab": [{"ko": "처음", "en": "first time, beginning"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 아니다", "exp": "Negative ''is not'': 처음이 아니에요 ''is not the first (time)''.", "example_in_sentence": "처음이 아니에요"}]}, {"text": "아빠는 전에 아기 엘라의 소리로도 음악을 만들었어요.", "translation": "Dad previously made music with baby Ella''s sounds too.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전에", "en": "before, previously"}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로도", "exp": "(으)로 ''with'' + 도 ''also'': 엘라의 소리로도 ''with baby Ella''s sounds too''.", "example_in_sentence": "소리로도"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "아빠", "en": "dad", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소리", "en": "sound", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모으다", "en": "to collect", "note": ""}, {"ko": "1년", "en": "one year", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동안", "en": "during", "note": ""}, {"ko": "녹음하다", "en": "to record", "note": ""}, {"ko": "록 음악", "en": "rock music", "note": ""}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make", "note": ""}, {"ko": "바꾸다", "en": "to change", "note": ""}, {"ko": "높낮이", "en": "pitch, tone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그대로", "en": "as is, unchanged", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쓰다", "en": "to use, to write", "note": ""}, {"ko": "개", "en": "counter for objects", "note": ""}, {"ko": "피아노", "en": "piano", "note": ""}, {"ko": "음", "en": "note, musical tone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to find", "note": ""}, {"ko": "맞추다", "en": "to match, to align", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아주", "en": "very, quite", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오래", "en": "long time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "걸리다", "en": "to take (time)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영상", "en": "video", "note": ""}, {"ko": "명", "en": "counter for people", "note": ""}, {"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed, to go over", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to watch, to see", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; to be a lot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "좋아하다", "en": "to like", "note": ""}, {"ko": "처음", "en": "first time, beginning", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전에", "en": "before, previously", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)로 (material)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Marks what something is made with: 그 소리로 음악을 만들다 ''make music with those sounds''.", "ex_ko": "아빠는 그 소리로 록 음악을 만들었어요.", "ex_en": "Dad made rock music from those sounds."}, {"name": "~지 않다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Negative ''did not'': 바꾸다 → 바꾸지 않았어요 ''didn''t change''.", "ex_ko": "아기 소리는 바꾸지 않았어요.", "ex_en": "The baby sounds were not changed."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''Can'': 쓰다 → 쓸 수 있다; as a noun modifier: 쓸 수 있는 소리 ''sounds that could be used''.", "ex_ko": "쓸 수 있는 소리는 83개였어요.", "ex_en": "There were 83 sounds that could be used."}, {"name": "~와/과 맞추다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''Match (something) to N'': 아기 소리와 맞추다 ''match (the notes) to the baby''s sounds''.", "ex_ko": "그리고 아기 소리와 맞췄어요.", "ex_en": "Then he matched them to the baby''s sounds."}, {"name": "~게", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Makes an adverb: 넘다 ''to exceed'' → 넘게 ''over / more than'': 1,100만 명이 넘게 ''more than 11 million people''.", "ex_ko": "영상을 1,100만 명이 넘게 봤어요.", "ex_en": "More than 11 million people watched the video."}, {"name": "~이/가 아니다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Negative ''is not'': 처음이 아니에요 ''is not the first (time)''.", "ex_ko": "이 아기 소리 음악은 처음이 아니에요.", "ex_en": "This isn''t his first music made from baby sounds."}, {"name": "~(으)로도", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "(으)로 ''with'' + 도 ''also'': 엘라의 소리로도 ''with baby Ella''s sounds too''.", "ex_ko": "아빠는 전에 아기 엘라의 소리로도 음악을 만들었어요.", "ex_en": "Dad previously made music with baby Ella''s sounds too."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mvslstigsmyc' and md5(translation) = 'ab54613279782858cdfa219c40fba392';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "일본의 똑똑한 기술자들이 특별한 것을 만들었어요.", "idx": 0, "translation": "Smart engineers from Japan made something special.", "vocab": [{"ko": "똑똑하다", "en": "smart, clever", "note": "adjective describing people or ideas"}, {"ko": "기술자", "en": "engineer, technician"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "special, particular"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ", "exp": "Past tense modifier describing the noun that follows", "example_in_sentence": "똑똑한 기술자들"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "몸에 착용할 수 있는 로봇 꼬리예요.", "idx": 1, "translation": "It is a robot tail that can be worn on the body.", "vocab": [{"ko": "착용하다", "en": "to wear, to put on", "note": "formal verb for wearing"}, {"ko": "로봇", "en": "robot"}, {"ko": "꼬리", "en": "tail"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Expresses possibility or ability", "example_in_sentence": "착용할 수 있는"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 로봇 꼬리는 할머니, 할아버지들을 도와줘요.", "idx": 2, "translation": "This robot tail helps elderly people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "할머니", "en": "grandmother; elderly woman"}, {"ko": "할아버지", "en": "grandfather; elderly man"}, {"ko": "도와주다", "en": "to help, to assist"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "걸을 때 넘어지지 않게 균형을 잡아줘요.", "idx": 3, "translation": "It maintains balance so that one doesn''t fall when walking.", "vocab": [{"ko": "넘어지다", "en": "to fall down, to tumble"}, {"ko": "균형", "en": "balance, equilibrium"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~지 않게", "exp": "Indicates prevention or negation of an action", "example_in_sentence": "넘어지지 않게"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "마치 동물의 꼬리처럼 움직여요.", "idx": 4, "translation": "It moves just like an animal''s tail.", "vocab": [{"ko": "동물", "en": "animal"}, {"ko": "마치", "en": "as if, just like"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~처럼", "exp": "Expresses similarity or comparison", "example_in_sentence": "동물의 꼬리처럼"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "한국도 고령화 사회(나이 많은 사람이 많은 사회)가 되고 있어요.", "idx": 5, "translation": "Korea is also becoming an aging society (a society with many elderly people).", "vocab": [{"ko": "고령화", "en": "aging, population aging"}, {"ko": "사회", "en": "society"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~어지다", "exp": "Expresses a change of state or becoming", "example_in_sentence": "고령화 사회가 되고"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이런 기술이 우리나라 어르신들에게도 도움이 될 것 같아요.", "idx": 6, "translation": "It seems like this technology will also be helpful to our country''s elderly people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기술", "en": "technology, technique"}, {"ko": "도움이 되다", "en": "to be helpful, to be useful"}, {"ko": "어르신", "en": "elderly person (honorific)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ 것 같다", "exp": "Expresses conjecture or supposition about the future", "example_in_sentence": "도움이 될 것 같아요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "앞으로 더 많은 로봇 기술이 나올 거예요.", "idx": 7, "translation": "Many more robot technologies will come out in the future.", "vocab": [{"ko": "앞으로", "en": "in the future, from now on"}, {"ko": "나오다", "en": "to come out, to emerge"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ 거다", "exp": "Expresses future tense with certainty or prediction", "example_in_sentence": "나올 거예요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "우리의 일상생활이 더 편해질 거예요.", "idx": 8, "translation": "Our daily life will become more comfortable.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일상생활", "en": "daily life, everyday life"}, {"ko": "편하다", "en": "comfortable, convenient"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~어지다", "exp": "Expresses a change of state or becoming", "example_in_sentence": "더 편해질 거예요"}], "analysis": []}]}', vocab = '[{"ko": "똑똑하다", "en": "smart, clever", "note": "adjective describing people or ideas"}, {"ko": "기술자", "en": "engineer, technician", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "special, particular", "note": ""}, {"ko": "착용하다", "en": "to wear, to put on", "note": "formal verb for wearing"}, {"ko": "로봇", "en": "robot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "꼬리", "en": "tail", "note": ""}, {"ko": "할머니", "en": "grandmother; elderly woman", "note": ""}, {"ko": "할아버지", "en": "grandfather; elderly man", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도와주다", "en": "to help, to assist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "넘어지다", "en": "to fall down, to tumble", "note": ""}, {"ko": "균형", "en": "balance, equilibrium", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동물", "en": "animal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마치", "en": "as if, just like", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고령화", "en": "aging, population aging", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사회", "en": "society", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기술", "en": "technology, technique", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도움이 되다", "en": "to be helpful, to be useful", "note": ""}, {"ko": "어르신", "en": "elderly person (honorific)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "앞으로", "en": "in the future, from now on", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나오다", "en": "to come out, to emerge", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일상생활", "en": "daily life, everyday life", "note": ""}, {"ko": "편하다", "en": "comfortable, convenient", "note": ""}, {"word": "균형을 잡다", "reading": "gyunhyeong-eul japda", "meaning": "to maintain balance; to keep in balance", "context": "균형을 잡아줘요."}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mon2iizudae8' and md5(translation) = '6d75fed1a557b0b55e8a3ff03b3e4d7b';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Iran has claimed that it attacked a U.S. Navy warship. However, U.S. authorities in Washington have strongly denied this.", "This incident could further worsen tensions in the Middle East region. The different positions between the two countries have become clearly apparent.", "The international community is concerned about such conflict situations. In particular, the possibility of maritime trade routes facing threats has increased.", "Experts emphasize that careful diplomatic resolution is necessary. This is a critical moment when dialogue is important to prevent military conflict."], "sentences": [{"text": "이란이 미국 해군 함정을 공격했다고 주장했습니다.", "translation": "Iran has claimed that it attacked a U.S. Navy warship.", "vocab": [{"ko": "주장하다", "en": "to claim; to assert", "note": "Often used for disputed or unverified statements in news contexts"}, {"ko": "해군", "en": "navy", "note": "Military branch; 해군 함정 = navy warship/vessel"}, {"ko": "함정", "en": "warship; naval vessel", "note": "Military ship; distinct from 배 (general ship)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~다고 주장하다", "exp": "Reports or conveys what someone has claimed; the complement clause precedes 주장하다", "example_in_sentence": "미국 해군 함정을 공격했다고 주장했습니다"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "하지만 미국 워싱턴 당국은 이를 강력히 부인했어요.", "translation": "However, U.S. authorities in Washington have strongly denied this.", "vocab": [{"ko": "당국", "en": "authorities; officials", "note": "Formal term for governmental bodies or official institutions"}, {"ko": "부인하다", "en": "to deny", "note": "Formal negation of a claim; 강력히 부인하다 = strongly deny"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ 수 있다 / ~어/아 있다 in perfect aspect", "exp": "The perfect aspect marker ~어 in 했어요 shows completed action with present relevance", "example_in_sentence": "부인했어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이번 사건은 중동 지역의 긴장 상황을 더욱 악화시킬 수 있습니다.", "translation": "This incident could further worsen tensions in the Middle East region.", "vocab": [{"ko": "긴장", "en": "tension; strain", "note": "Often paired with 상황 (situation) in political/military contexts"}, {"ko": "악화시키다", "en": "to worsen; to aggravate", "note": "Causative form of 악화되다; takes direct object"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Expresses possibility or potential; future or conditional sense", "example_in_sentence": "악화시킬 수 있습니다"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "양국 간의 입장 차이가 명확하게 드러났어요.", "translation": "The different positions between the two countries have become clearly apparent.", "vocab": [{"ko": "입장", "en": "position; stance; standpoint", "note": "Political/diplomatic viewpoint; 입장 차이 = difference in positions"}, {"ko": "드러나다", "en": "to become apparent; to be revealed", "note": "Intransitive; describes something becoming visible or clear"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~게 드러나다", "exp": "The adverbial suffix ~게 modifies how the action unfolds; 명확하게 = clearly", "example_in_sentence": "명확하게 드러났어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "국제 사회는 이런 갈등 상황을 우려하고 있습니다.", "translation": "The international community is concerned about such conflict situations.", "vocab": [{"ko": "국제 사회", "en": "international community", "note": "Collective term for nations and global actors"}, {"ko": "우려하다", "en": "to be concerned; to worry", "note": "Formal; expresses concern about a situation"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect; ongoing state or action in present time", "example_in_sentence": "우려하고 있습니다"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "특히 해상 교통로의 안전이 위협받을 가능성이 높아졌어요.", "translation": "In particular, the possibility of maritime trade routes facing threats has increased.", "vocab": [{"ko": "해상 교통로", "en": "maritime trade route; sea lane", "note": "Compound noun; 해상 = maritime, 교통로 = route/corridor"}, {"ko": "위협받다", "en": "to be threatened; to face a threat", "note": "Passive/middle voice form; indicates receiving or facing a threat"}, {"ko": "가능성", "en": "possibility; likelihood", "note": "Abstract noun; 가능성이 높아지다 = possibility increases"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ 가능성", "exp": "The modifier ~ㄹ with 가능성 expresses potential or likelihood of an event", "example_in_sentence": "위협받을 가능성"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "전문가들은 신중한 외교적 해결이 필요하다고 강조합니다.", "translation": "Experts emphasize that careful diplomatic resolution is necessary.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist", "note": "Person with deep knowledge in a field"}, {"ko": "신중하다", "en": "to be careful; cautious; prudent", "note": "Adjective describing deliberate, thoughtful approach"}, {"ko": "해결", "en": "resolution; settlement", "note": "Noun; 외교적 해결 = diplomatic resolution"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~다고 강조하다", "exp": "Reports emphasis on a statement; the complement clause precedes the reporting verb", "example_in_sentence": "필요하다고 강조합니다"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "무력 충돌로 이어지지 않도록 대화가 중요한 시점이에요.", "translation": "This is a critical moment when dialogue is important to prevent military conflict.", "vocab": [{"ko": "무력 충돌", "en": "military conflict; armed clash", "note": "Compound noun; 무력 = military force, 충돌 = collision/conflict"}, {"ko": "이어지다", "en": "to lead to; to be connected to; to result in", "note": "Often used to show a chain of cause-effect; negative contexts with ~지 않도록"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~지 않도록", "exp": "Expresses purpose or intention to prevent something; literally ''so as not to''", "example_in_sentence": "무력 충돌로 이어지지 않도록"}], "analysis": []}]}', vocab = '[{"ko": "주장하다", "en": "to claim; to assert", "note": "Often used for disputed or unverified statements in news contexts"}, {"ko": "해군", "en": "navy", "note": "Military branch; 해군 함정 = navy warship/vessel"}, {"ko": "함정", "en": "warship; naval vessel", "note": "Military ship; distinct from 배 (general ship)"}, {"ko": "당국", "en": "authorities; officials", "note": "Formal term for governmental bodies or official institutions"}, {"ko": "부인하다", "en": "to deny", "note": "Formal negation of a claim; 강력히 부인하다 = strongly deny"}, {"ko": "긴장", "en": "tension; strain", "note": "Often paired with 상황 (situation) in political/military contexts"}, {"ko": "악화시키다", "en": "to worsen; to aggravate", "note": "Causative form of 악화되다; takes direct object"}, {"ko": "입장", "en": "position; stance; standpoint", "note": "Political/diplomatic viewpoint; 입장 차이 = difference in positions"}, {"ko": "드러나다", "en": "to become apparent; to be revealed", "note": "Intransitive; describes something becoming visible or clear"}, {"ko": "국제 사회", "en": "international community", "note": "Collective term for nations and global actors"}, {"ko": "우려하다", "en": "to be concerned; to worry", "note": "Formal; expresses concern about a situation"}, {"ko": "해상 교통로", "en": "maritime trade route; sea lane", "note": "Compound noun; 해상 = maritime, 교통로 = route/corridor"}, {"ko": "위협받다", "en": "to be threatened; to face a threat", "note": "Passive/middle voice form; indicates receiving or facing a threat"}, {"ko": "가능성", "en": "possibility; likelihood", "note": "Abstract noun; 가능성이 높아지다 = possibility increases"}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist", "note": "Person with deep knowledge in a field"}, {"ko": "신중하다", "en": "to be careful; cautious; prudent", "note": "Adjective describing deliberate, thoughtful approach"}, {"ko": "해결", "en": "resolution; settlement", "note": "Noun; 외교적 해결 = diplomatic resolution"}, {"ko": "무력 충돌", "en": "military conflict; armed clash", "note": "Compound noun; 무력 = military force, 충돌 = collision/conflict"}, {"ko": "이어지다", "en": "to lead to; to be connected to; to result in", "note": "Often used to show a chain of cause-effect; negative contexts with ~지 않도록"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mor761zdqa7r' and md5(translation) = 'f3cc85cc61eb18866630052ce1a6a75d';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In 1907, Australian swimmer Annette Kellerman fought for women''s rights. She advocated for the right to wear a fitted one-piece swimsuit.", "At that time, women had to swim in heavy clothing like long skirts and blouses. Kellerman thought such clothes were dangerous and uncomfortable. So she appeared in public wearing a fitted one-piece swimsuit.", "However, society could not accept her actions. Police arrested Kellerman on charges of indecency. At that time, people considered it inappropriate for women to reveal the contours of their bodies.", "Kellerman''s brave challenge later led to changes in women''s fashion. The swimsuits we wear today originated from her efforts. She was a pioneer who fought against social prejudice for women''s freedom and practicality."], "sentences": [{"text": "1907년 호주 출신 수영 선수 애니트 켈러맨이 여성의 권리를 위해 싸웠어요.", "translation": "In 1907, Australian swimmer Annette Kellerman fought for women''s rights.", "vocab": [{"ko": "출신", "en": "origin/native of", "note": "Marks where someone or something comes from; often used with place names"}, {"ko": "수영 선수", "en": "swimmer", "note": "Compound: 수영 (swimming) + 선수 (athlete)"}, {"ko": "싸우다", "en": "to fight/struggle", "note": "Can be literal combat or figurative struggle for a cause"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ (past modifying adjective)", "exp": "Modifies a noun with a past-tense meaning; here 호주 출신 is treated as fixed expression but 싸웠어요 is simple past", "example_in_sentence": "호주 출신 (Australian, origin-marked)"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그녀는 몸에 맞는 원피스 수영복을 입을 권리를 주장했습니다.", "translation": "She advocated for the right to wear a fitted one-piece swimsuit.", "vocab": [{"ko": "몸에 맞다", "en": "to fit the body", "note": "~에 맞다 means ''to fit/suit''; here applied to clothing fitting properly"}, {"ko": "원피스", "en": "one-piece (swimsuit)", "note": "Loanword from English; refers to single continuous garment"}, {"ko": "주장하다", "en": "to advocate/claim", "note": "Formal verb meaning to assert or argue for something"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ 권리", "exp": "Creates ''the right to [verb]'' by adding 권리 (right) after future-tense modifying form", "example_in_sentence": "입을 권리 (the right to wear)"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "당시 여성들은 긴 치마와 블라우스 같은 무거운 옷으로 수영을 해야 했어요.", "translation": "At that time, women had to swim in heavy clothing like long skirts and blouses.", "vocab": [{"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time/back then", "note": "Formal/written adverb; refers to a specific past period"}, {"ko": "치마", "en": "skirt", "note": "Standard word for skirt garment"}, {"ko": "무겁다", "en": "to be heavy", "note": "Adjective describing weight or burden"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~어야 하다 (obligation/necessity)", "exp": "Expresses what one had to do or was required to do", "example_in_sentence": "수영을 해야 했어요 (had to swim)"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "켈러맨은 이런 옷이 위험하고 불편하다고 생각했습니다.", "translation": "Kellerman thought such clothes were dangerous and uncomfortable.", "vocab": [{"ko": "위험하다", "en": "to be dangerous", "note": "Adjective describing something that poses risk or danger"}, {"ko": "불편하다", "en": "to be inconvenient/uncomfortable", "note": "Adjective meaning lacking convenience or comfort"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 (conjunction joining adjectives)", "exp": "Connects two adjectives/descriptors in sequence; ''and'' in English", "example_in_sentence": "위험하고 불편하다 (dangerous and uncomfortable)"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그래서 몸에 딱 맞는 원피스 수영복을 입고 공개적으로 나타났어요.", "translation": "So she appeared in public wearing a fitted one-piece swimsuit.", "vocab": [{"ko": "딱", "en": "exactly/snugly/tightly", "note": "Adverb emphasizing precise fit; intensifies 맞다 here"}, {"ko": "공개적으로", "en": "publicly/openly", "note": "Adverb form of 공개적 (public); emphasizes visibility and boldness"}, {"ko": "나타나다", "en": "to appear/emerge", "note": "Intransitive verb meaning to become visible or show up"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 (joining two actions in sequence)", "exp": "Connects two actions performed by the same subject; ''and'' or ''while doing''", "example_in_sentence": "입고 나타났어요 (wore [and] appeared)"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "하지만 사회는 그녀의 행동을 받아들이지 못했어요.", "translation": "However, society could not accept her actions.", "vocab": [{"ko": "받아들이다", "en": "to accept/receive", "note": "Verb meaning to take in or accept something offered"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~지 못하다 (negation of ability/possibility)", "exp": "Expresses inability or failure to do something; stronger than 안 하다", "example_in_sentence": "받아들이지 못했어요 (could not accept)"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "경찰은 켈러맨을 품위를 해친 죄로 체포했습니다.", "translation": "Police arrested Kellerman on charges of indecency.", "vocab": [{"ko": "경찰", "en": "police", "note": "Noun; law enforcement authority"}, {"ko": "품위를 해치다", "en": "to damage/violate decency", "note": "Phrase: 품위 (dignity/decorum) + 해치다 (to harm); idiom meaning breach of propriety"}, {"ko": "죄", "en": "crime/charge/guilt", "note": "Noun; often follows ~로 (on the charge of)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ 죄로 (reason/charge expressed as noun phrase)", "exp": "Uses past-tense modifier + 죄로 to express ''on the charge of'' or ''for the crime of''", "example_in_sentence": "품위를 해친 죄로 (on charges of indecency)"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "당시 사람들은 여성이 몸의 선을 드러내는 것을 부적절하다고 여겼어요.", "translation": "At that time, people considered it inappropriate for women to reveal the contours of their bodies.", "vocab": [{"ko": "선", "en": "line/contour/outline", "note": "Noun; here means body silhouette or curves"}, {"ko": "드러내다", "en": "to reveal/expose", "note": "Verb meaning to make visible or uncover"}, {"ko": "부적절하다", "en": "to be inappropriate/unsuitable", "note": "Formal adjective; opposite of 적절하다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~는 것을 ~라고 여기다 (perception/judgment expression)", "exp": "Expresses what people think or consider something to be; 여기다 means ''to regard''", "example_in_sentence": "드러내는 것을 부적절하다고 여겼어요 (considered [it] inappropriate)"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "켈러맨의 용감한 도전은 후에 여성 패션의 변화를 이끌었어요.", "translation": "Kellerman''s brave challenge later led to changes in women''s fashion.", "vocab": [{"ko": "용감하다", "en": "to be brave/courageous", "note": "Adjective meaning showing courage"}, {"ko": "도전", "en": "challenge", "note": "Noun; an act of challenging or confronting"}, {"ko": "이끌다", "en": "to lead/bring about", "note": "Verb; to guide or cause something to happen"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~은/는 후에 (after; temporal expression)", "exp": "Marks a point in time following a prior action; 후 (after) is more formal than 다음에", "example_in_sentence": "후에 (later; after)"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "오늘날 우리가 입는 수영복의 시작이 바로 그녀의 노력에서 비롯되었습니다.", "translation": "The swimsuits we wear today originated from her efforts.", "vocab": [{"ko": "오늘날", "en": "today/nowadays", "note": "Formal adverb; contrast with casual 요즘"}, {"ko": "시작", "en": "beginning/origin", "note": "Noun; the point where something begins"}, {"ko": "비롯되다", "en": "to originate/stem from", "note": "Passive verb; means ''to have its origin in''"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~에서 비롯되다 (source/origin marker)", "exp": "Expresses that something originates or stems from a source; 에서 marks the origin", "example_in_sentence": "그녀의 노력에서 비롯되었습니다 (originated from her efforts)"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그녀는 여성의 자유와 실용성을 위해 사회적 편견과 맞서 싸운 선구자였어요.", "translation": "She was a pioneer who fought against social prejudice for women''s freedom and practicality.", "vocab": [{"ko": "선구자", "en": "pioneer/trailblazer", "note": "Noun; someone who initiates or leads the way"}, {"ko": "편견", "en": "prejudice/bias", "note": "Noun; preconceived judgment or bias"}, {"ko": "실용성", "en": "practicality/usefulness", "note": "Noun; the quality of being practical or functional"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ (past modifying relative clause)", "exp": "Creates a relative clause modifying 선구자; 싸운 (who fought) describes the noun", "example_in_sentence": "싸운 선구자 (a pioneer who fought)"}], "analysis": []}]}', vocab = '[{"ko": "출신", "en": "origin/native of", "note": "Marks where someone or something comes from; often used with place names"}, {"ko": "수영 선수", "en": "swimmer", "note": "Compound: 수영 (swimming) + 선수 (athlete)"}, {"ko": "싸우다", "en": "to fight/struggle", "note": "Can be literal combat or figurative struggle for a cause"}, {"ko": "몸에 맞다", "en": "to fit the body", "note": "~에 맞다 means ''to fit/suit''; here applied to clothing fitting properly"}, {"ko": "원피스", "en": "one-piece (swimsuit)", "note": "Loanword from English; refers to single continuous garment"}, {"ko": "주장하다", "en": "to advocate/claim", "note": "Formal verb meaning to assert or argue for something"}, {"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time/back then", "note": "Formal/written adverb; refers to a specific past period"}, {"ko": "치마", "en": "skirt", "note": "Standard word for skirt garment"}, {"ko": "무겁다", "en": "to be heavy", "note": "Adjective describing weight or burden"}, {"ko": "위험하다", "en": "to be dangerous", "note": "Adjective describing something that poses risk or danger"}, {"ko": "불편하다", "en": "to be inconvenient/uncomfortable", "note": "Adjective meaning lacking convenience or comfort"}, {"ko": "딱", "en": "exactly/snugly/tightly", "note": "Adverb emphasizing precise fit; intensifies 맞다 here"}, {"ko": "공개적으로", "en": "publicly/openly", "note": "Adverb form of 공개적 (public); emphasizes visibility and boldness"}, {"ko": "나타나다", "en": "to appear/emerge", "note": "Intransitive verb meaning to become visible or show up"}, {"ko": "받아들이다", "en": "to accept/receive", "note": "Verb meaning to take in or accept something offered"}, {"ko": "경찰", "en": "police", "note": "Noun; law enforcement authority"}, {"ko": "품위를 해치다", "en": "to damage/violate decency", "note": "Phrase: 품위 (dignity/decorum) + 해치다 (to harm); idiom meaning breach of propriety"}, {"ko": "죄", "en": "crime/charge/guilt", "note": "Noun; often follows ~로 (on the charge of)"}, {"ko": "선", "en": "line/contou